Well, considering how much trouble I had getting OSF/1 working on the Alpha
I've got here at first I wonder what their classification of "developer's
version" and "production quality" is -- I had to go through some pretty nasty
hoops to get the firmware updated on this thing to install V1.2 -- anyone
else have to use their firmware CD-ROM (complete with its VMS filesystem on
a Unix box and 'cat' the raw device to find out the proper directory name
that the update stuff was kept in?  (I was given instructions for the 1.1
firmware upgrade, not the version 2 firmware that was contained on the CD-ROM,
and they changed things around!)

Seriously though, once the initial problems were past I've had no problem with
V1.2 in couple weeks I've had it.  But V1.0 on the MIPS box was surprisingly
solid as well, though there were problems that it didn't work with the 3D
graphics card they gave us, and we had to drop to a lowly 8 bit card to get it
to work.

I can't imagine that they haven't been keeping their MIPS port up to date,
though I'm sure some of the older hardware doesn't have drivers.  Probably
their decision has something to do with the idea that they can't support MIPS
halfway and say 'only these configurations are supported' (it'd be like using
a PC instead of a workstation!)  But I can't believe it'd be that difficult
to port their drivers -- they money they'd get by people upgrading from Ultrix
would probably fund that work.

