In article <1993Mar24.144141.48433@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu>, rsl11@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu writes:
>
>Hello there,
>
>	I have a question concerning the loading and mounting of a magnaetic
>tape using the VMS system. I have a roundreel tape 6250BPI(bits per inch),
>2400ft long, with records of variable length. When I mount it what should I
>specify for record length since it the record length is variable.

Use
	MOUNT/FOREIGN/BLOCK=62536/RECORD=62536 MTxx:
This specifies the _maximum_ physical record length (/BLOCK) and the maximum
logical record length (/RECORD).

>	Also, how do I copy the tape to hard disk? Can I simply use the copy
>command to copy the tape? I do not think that the tape is an ANSI tape.

Yes, COPY is all that is needed.  Mount the tape as above, then issue the
command
	COPY/LOG MTxx: filename

This same technique can be used for tape-to-tape copying.  Just MOUNT the
output tape in the same manner as the input tape and specify the output drive
in place of the "filename".

