I've been working with a customer of ours who has a Datability VCP-1000 running
V3.302 software.  We are currently having problems printing to it.  TGV has
helped us narrow it down to a protocol problem if two print jobs get fired to
it in rapid succession.  The server acknowledges the request to start the
second job (while the printer is still finishing the first job).  When we start
to send data, the server changes its mind, issues a RST, and throws the data
it's already received into the bitbucket.

Our network group has been actively trying to contact Datability on behalf of
the customer.  Datability is simply not returning any phone calls and the
customer is still unable to print.

If you decide to purchase your Datability server, I hope that you don't need
customer support or that the service organization in the US is better than it
is Canada.

