  As far as I know Datability has no customer service organization in
Canada, so I presume it's the New York office of Datability that your
network group is having the problem with. One could then assume that a
customer in the US can expect the same level of support. Datability does
seem to rely on their dealers to provide some amount of support, of the
two dealer in the area I've dealt with one was completely useless in
terms of support and one is pretty good.

  My experience has been somewhat similar. I have had a long standing
problem with the way Datability implements DTRWAIT on their non-modem-control
cards. After going around in circles with then on this under an earlier
version of the VCP-1000 software they finally decided it worked the way
they intended and I was out of luck. Then in the latest version of the
software they documented the behaviour of DTRWAIT, and the documentation
matched the behaviour I wanted, but the server still exhibited the old
behaviour. Again after a long delay they decided that the new documentation
was wrong and the server still behaved as intended.

  In general, I'd say that when Datability equipment works it
works quite well ( ie things that work are fairly solid - it doesn't
exhibit flaky behaviour ), but when you have a problem be prepared to spend
a lot of your own time diagnosing it, and to finally find out there's
nothing you can do about it.

