We've got a problem with our DECsystem 5500 that I don't know how to
solve. We're running Ultrix 4.2.

We have got some modems hooked directly to the computer, managed by
getty. For some reason, when you connect to the modem you have to wait
some amount of time (10 or 20 seconds, typically) before you get a
login prompt. Once logged in everything works fine.

I don't quite understand the magic of modems and UNIX machines, but
reading man pages it looks like what's going on is that the only way
Ultrix recognizes that a modem has connected to it is that getty wakes
up once a minute to see if its connection is live.

This seems pretty silly to me. Shouldn't the modem be informing
someone that it's been connected to, which should then wake up getty
which runs login? Event based, instead of polling?

I've been told that our DECsystem 5500 lacks the necessary hardware to
do this, and that the "check once a minute" is the best you can do. Is
this really true?

