dataram@tigger.jvnc.net (Dataram Corp. PO Box 7528) writes:

> This must be stupid question #1,234,567, but let me ask it anyway. I habe
> both TK50 and TK70 tape drives. After a blank tape is initialized using
> a TK50 drive, I cant't make backups on that tape using a TK70 drive. Is
> there anyway to "re-initialize" a tape?
> (I'm getting this second hand from our technicial, and it does not make
> sence to me).

OK, it's really quite simple and follows only two rules:

1) If you have a totally virgin tape, the first drive you stick it into is
the one who's format it becomes. 

2) You can't format at virgin TK70 in a TK50 drive.

Which is another way of saying the tapes are unformatted and the drive has
the format logic but can't format the newer drive density.

Therefore, if you put a unformatted TK50 in a TK70 drive, the resulting tape
can only be read on TK70's. 

-dhan



