> Has anybody any experience with TDK or similar tapes for backing up
> 2.0Gbytes on a single tape?
> 
> 	I was just talking to our Australian supplier who offered me
> two types of DAT tape for data use, 1 for 1.2Gb and the other a double 
> length tape capable of storing 2.0Gbytes.

If your DAT drive is a TLZ04 then I strongly reccomend you stick with 1.3Gb
tapes (these are 60 meters long).  The TLZ04 cannot properly handle 2.0Gbyte
taprs (which are 90 meters long). The reason it can't halndle them is the 
different tape thickness, which requires different tension control. Whilst 
2.0Gbyte tapes might "seem to work", you are risking data loss. 

Note that this comment applies only to TLZ04 and other "early" DAT drives.
If you have a newer model then 60 or 90m will do.

Regarding actual tape quality: HP reccomends that people only
use DDS branded media. Some audio media is of poor quality and can result in
data loss and (in the worst case) tape jamms in drives. 

