>/dev/rz0b: No such device

This suggests that you aren't running the kernel that has the configuration
line below.  Did you build a new kernel after making the modification and
then boot it?

On a DEC{system,station} you can look at the swap table using dbx.  Look
to see how many entires you have:

# dbx -k /vmunix /dev/mem
(dbx) print swdevt[0]
struct {
    sw_dev = 5377
    sw_freed = 1
    sw_nblks = 184320
    sw_type = 0
    sw_gnodeptr = (nil)
    sw_strat = (nil)
    sw_priority = 0
    sw_nio = 58872
}

The last entry in the table will be all zeros.  If swdevt[1] is the last
entry, then you clearly aren't running the kernel you think you are.

