I'll fess up, ... I, I am a closet DEC VAX junkie... at home....  I
have a VAX 11/730-ZA down in the basement holding the floor down but
is (now) powered off, it was the -ZA config with an R80/RL02 with RB730/IDC
disk controller, 4 MB of MS730-CA (actually MS750-CA) memory, a DMF32,
and a TS11, oh yea I have two of them (one for spare parts of course).
It probably still boots, if only I would put the 50 conductor SMD ribbon
cable back between the RB730 and the R80 disk.  I remember it fondly dimming
the lights wildly as the TS11 tensioned the tape during reads, and the R80
dimming the lights quite significantly as it spun the platter up.  All
of this was running in an apartment I rented some years ago.  God I love'd
to watch that thing boot its individual microcode files from TU58's
(BASIC, QUEUE, IDC, etc)... teaching those 8 AMD2901 bit slice processors
how to be a VAX.

I once almost took possession of an HP3000 Series III (old kind in tall
cabinet with blinking lights atop), but decided agsinst it (wisely)...
lots of power and not very versatile OS wise, although at the time I
was heavily into MPE.  Talked a friend into buying a couple of
HP "mighty mice" (HP3000/37's, HP's equiv to the MicroVAX II in the HP3000
world) both for $950 recently, was a good deal.

Now I run a rather fully configured VAXstation II/GPX (MicroVAX II with
GPX accelerator set) in the BA123 "world box" enclosure, it has the
full 16MB of memory (2 MS630-CA compatibles), DEQNA (works great though),
DHV11 8 port asynch mux (not used really), VCB02-C (GPX) 8 plane total
graphics, VR290-DA "tune'd up" & LK201 & VSXXX-AA puck mouse, QT13
pertec to QBUS TMSCP controller talking to a CDC639 1600/6250 9-track
(this is the drive DEC used as the TU81, but pertec interface), TQK50/TK50,
and an EMULEX QD32 SMD to QBUS MSCP controller talking to two Fujitsu
M2333 (approx 274MB each formatted) disks.  Oh yea there is a nice
room-fan that runs constantly in front of the system to keep the air
circulating so it doesn't all melt-down, but with it things are fine.
The house (actually one room at this point) has an ethernet which
my wife's PC is also on, and both the VAX and it get to the rest of
the world 24hrs a day via a 286 PC clone running a specially hacked version
of PCROUTE 2.22 to another such PC at work.  The changes I made
to PCROUTE a long with some scripts using PROCOMM make the setup
fault tolerant with two V.32 MODEM's using normal phone lines that
just stay up all the time.  Any line drops that occur (infrequent,
maybe one every few days) are recovered from and the link is back up
within 1-2 minutes without any intervention.  Oh yea, I have 3 small
UPS's that keep it all running, providing about 7 minutes of reserve
power when the electric goes out (or small power glitches).  Ah...
the times I've had to stagger into the computer-den in total
darkness from bed with UPS's blarring at many decibals, powering
up the VR290 to signon and get the system shutdown... but it all works!
Also have the TK50 doing automatic incremental backups every morning
by itself... tape needs changing once every 3 weeks or so...

Future?  An upgrade to a KA650 and MS650 memory when I can afford it,
the KA630 isn't great for DECwindows in terms of turnaround time,
but it isn't unusable either.

Stories?  I did know someone who had a DEC-10 in their 10th floor
highrise apartment's living room.  Saw it, very impressive.  Filled
(or lined I should say) all the walls in what was a very large living
room.  You reading this Doug? :-)

