The only X port for the Amiga is the one from GfxBase.  Fortunately, it's
excellent.  A server-only option is available, if all you need is a display
device.  Twm and olwm are standard, and mwm is an option.

There are two implementations of SLIP for the Amiga.  One is a port of the
KA9Q package from MS-DOS, but the Amiga X server isn't compatible with it.
The other is part of the beta version of the Amiga AS225 TCP/IP package,
which GfxBase can supply to you.

