Don,

What is the DECnet pipeline quota on your VMS systems?  DEC was
usually overstating the requirements for early DECwindows performance
when they recommended a minimum pipeline quota of 10000.  On many of our
systems the systems managers assumed that more was better, so they made
this even larger.

However, some ethernet controllers can not handle the large amounts of
packets coming at them, so the host system must send them again.

I think there has been some discussion about this in some of the DEC-related
trade rags recently, and maybe even something in Quorum...?

At any rate, we determined that setting the pipeline quota on our systems
back to 4032 improved the x-windows performance to these slower ethernet
controllers.

Hope this helps.


