>This must be stupid question #1,234,567, but let me ask it anyway. I habe
>both TK50 and TK70 tape drives. After a blank tape is initialized using
>a TK50 drive, I cant't make backups on that tape using a TK70 drive. Is
>there anyway to "re-initialize" a tape?
>(I'm getting this second hand from our technicial, and it does not make
>sence to me).

Get a large magnet.  Formatted tapes aren't interchangeable for writing,
but a TK70 will read a TK50 tape.  If you have CompacTape I tapes (TK50),
you'll need to bulk erase them to use them on a TK70.  Don't be surprised
if there is an increase in the number of soft errors when using TK50
tapes on a TK70 either.  The tapes used by the TK70 are higher quality
than the TK50 tapes.  The bulk erase trick isn't supported either, use
it at your own risk and at the risk of losing the data you write on
those tapes.

