> One of the crystals on the HX card is in a socket. If you change that crystal
> to a 119.843 Mhz crystal, you can use your old monitor.
> 
There are various HX variants, all of which support the default 1280x1024x72HZ.
All HX's will support one other screen resolution and frame rate, depending on the
jumper on the card.  The second resolution/frame rate is determined by one of the 
crystals on the card.  Note that the operating system and X server will reconfigure
itself automatically (the on board rom figures out what to do at boot time, and
the operating system similarly figures out the screen resolution.  So easiest is
to get the proper variant of the card.  If you can't you can change out the crystal.

Note the crystals can be somewhat hard to come by and you should get
the same type as on the board; they needed to be to be able to run at the top speed
without any video problems.
				- Jim Gettys



