>Are those Release notes somewhere on an upgraded machine ? Or do i have
>to search for a printed book ?

The release notes are printed and are included with the upgrade media in
the upgrade kit.

>BTW, is there no chance to use it correctly with XPrompter ?

You can use MIT-MAGIC-COOKIE without using Xdm (i.e. yes you can use it with
Xprompter).  However, depending on how your workstation is used Xdm might
be more convenient.  Xdm will generate a new authorization for you and
communicate it to the server every time you log in.  If you use Xprompter,
then you have to generate an authorization (as often as you think necessary),
and you must tell the server to use it using the "-auth" option.
