We have used DAT tapes on our SGI machines for nearly a year now.

The first tapes we bought were from SGI. They were normal Audio quality
60 minutes (not meters) BASF tapes. You could store approx. 600 Mb on
one tape, and they cost a fortune! We fould the same kind of tape in the
local radio shop (Kenwood HiFi Center, Falkoner Alle), however they
were 120 minutes (still not meters), and cost 69 dKr a piece (approx
10.5 US$).

All the data we store are stored in duplicates.

We have never had any read errors on these tapes.

I don't think you can retension a DAT tape. If you issue the mt retension
command, it returns immediately. I think this command is only relevant for
the 1/4" tapes, as they have the tape driven by a rubber band.

