One of the development groups on a project I am working on did some
performance testing with POSIX on an OpenVMS 5.5 platform.  They found
that using POSIX resulted in about a 60 times performance slowdown,
ie, programs that took 1 second under VMS without POSIX took about 1
minute under VMS with POSIX.  In one case, a program that took 1
minute under VMS without POSIX took over 1 hour under VMS with POSIX.
When POSIX was used, the programs were rewritten to use the POSIX
calls.  

We were told that DEC is working on this problem.  In the meantime,
are there any performance hacks or development techniques that I could
pass on to the development team?  We would like the system to be POSIX
compatible if possible.

Barry Smith
bds@mbunix.mitre.org



