| >of DAT tapes, ie.
| 
| > - How many times can a tape be read/written ?

Data grade is good for 2000-5000 passes across the heads (number
depends on drive and media vendor claims).

| > - How long is data guaranteed to be readable ?

At least 10 years for data grade, but that is all accelerated life testing.

| > - How should a written tape be stored (temperature/humidity) ?

See the enclosures in most of the tapes.

| > - Is it necessary to retension a stored tape (eg. once a month) ?
| 
| We have used DAT tapes on our SGI machines for nearly a year now.
