kam@dlogics.com (Kevin A. Mitchell) writes:

>We have a DecStation 5100 running Ultrix 4.2. It won't page out. There's
>72Mb of physical memory, and 65Mb of swap space. pstat -s shows that the
>swap space is present and not used, and vmstat -s shows that while there
>have been page ins (probably due to running programs), there have not
>been any page outs.

>Does anybody have any idea what the problem could be? Other 4.2 systems
>seem to be working just fine.

What is the problem? You should be happy that no page-outs occur, while
page-ins are normal due to demand-paging.
This just means that the amount of memory is sufficient for you applictions.
A Problem could be the size of your swap space, as a good rule of thumb says,
let the swap space be two to three times of the physical memory size.

